  "idea": {
    "tipo": "pedido",
    "premisa": "Movies vs Reality, 5 myths about being the last person on Earth, narrated in second person. The structure is myth, then reality, instead of a time countdown. Myth 1: 'You'd have free electricity forever.' Reality: most of the grid goes dark within hours to days with no one running the plants; only dams like Hoover could keep producing longer. Myth 2: 'You'd drive any Ferrari you want.' Reality: gasoline goes stale in roughly 6 to 12 months, so you end up on a bicycle. Myth 3: 'Supermarkets are endless food.' Reality: fresh food rots in weeks; canned food lasts for years, and honey basically never spoils. Myth 4: 'Cities would look like the movie, intact.' Reality: New York's subway pumps remove about 13 million gallons of water a day, and without them the tunnels could flood in about 36 hours. Myth 5: 'The real danger is wild animals.' Reality: the worst threat is loneliness; studies link chronic social isolation to health risks comparable to smoking 15 cigarettes a day. Finally, the twist.",
    "gancho": "What if you were the last person on Earth? Hollywood got almost everything wrong. Here are 5 myths that would get you killed.",
    "giro_final": "But here's the thing no movie tells you. You're the last person ON Earth, not the last human. Right now there are usually around 10 people orbiting above you on the International Space Station and China's Tiangong station. And their capsules can bring them home. So look up. Someone might be landing to find you.",
    "estilo_visual": "Dominated by 'composicion', with a myth/reality pattern in every block. Each myth opens with a sunny 'escena' in the style of a Hollywood dream: you in an empty Times Square, then you behind the wheel of a sports car. The reality then lands with an 'accion' or a 'composicion' that breaks it. A city street with a power pole and lights shutting off one by one. The 'deportivo' piece with a gas pump and the person pedaling a bicycle. A supermarket with rotting fruit next to stacked cans and a honey jar. A subway tunnel with water rising. Use 'big_text' only for '36 HOURS' and '15 CIGARETTES A DAY'. Show loneliness with 'accion' (llorar, gritar) in an empty plaza. For the twist, cut to 'space' with the ISS crossing over Earth, then 'accion' sorpresa as the person looks at the sky at night.",
    "por_que_funcionara": "It copies the formula of two approved videos ('Movies vs Reality' and '5 Myths vs Reality'). It also avoids the timeline that made the owner reject the 1,000-year version. Each myth feeds a fantasy the viewer has had (free mansions, free cars) and then destroys it with a surprising, verifiable fact, which keeps people watching to the next myth. The ISS twist challenges the title itself and invites comments ('I never thought of that'). It also creates a natural loop: the last line, 'look up', ties back to the opening question.",
